$+comments
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------%0D%0AProfile Wizard Coefficient Revision 2.9 Release Notes:%0D%0A----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------%0D%0AI. General:%0D%0A1. This is the second release of the ZL88702 worldwide coefficients.%0D%0A2. This release includes support for the following 44 countries:%0D%0AArgentina (AR), Austria (AT), Australia (AU), Belgium (BE), Brazil (BR), Bulgaria (BG), Canada (CA), Switzerland (CH),%0D%0AChile (CL), China (CN), Czech Republic (CZ), Germany (DE), Denmark (DK), Ecuador (EC), Spain (ES), Finland (FI),%0D%0AFrance (FR), UK (GB), Greece (GR), Hong Kong SAR China (HK), Hungary (HU), Indonesia (ID), Ireland (IE), Israel (IL),%0D%0AIndia (IN), Iceland (IS), Italy (IT), Japan (JP), S. Korea (KR), Mexico (MX), Malaysia (MY), Netherlands (NL),%0D%0ANorway (NO), New Zealand (NZ), Poland (PL), Portugal (PT), Russian Federation (RU), Sweden (SE), Singapore (SG),%0D%0AThailand (TH), Turkey (TK), Taiwan (TW), USA (US), and South Africa (ZA).%0D%0A2. The coefficients in this and all releases are provided for use only with the Microsemi VoicePath API-II (VP-API-II). Please refer %0D%0Ato the terms and conditions for licensing the software regarding terms and conditions of usage. These profiles are provided for %0D%0Areference only with no guarantee whatsoever by Microsemi Corporation.%0D%0A3. This release is for the ZLR88721H SM2 Line Module based on the ZL88702.%0D%0A%0D%0AII. Device Profile:%0D%0A1. The default settings for the Device Profile are:%0D%0A       PCLK = 8192 kHz%0D%0A       PCM Transmit Edge = Positive%0D%0A       Transmit Time Slot = 0%0D%0A       Receive Time Slot = 0%0D%0A       Interrupt Mode = Open Drain%0D%0A       Switcher = Flyback (12V in / 135V out)%0D%0A       IO21 Pin Mode = Analog Voltage Sense%0D%0A       IO22 Pin Mode = Digital%0D%0A    %0D%0A2. The settings may be changed by the user as necessary.  Please refer to the ZL880 and VP-API-II documentation for information %0D%0Aabout the supported settings.%0D%0A%0D%0AII. DC Profiles:%0D%0A1. The DC_FXS_ZL880_FB150V_DEF Profile is the default unless a country specific profile is selected. Example DC profile settings are%0D%0Aprovided for China, ETSI and the USA.%0D%0A%0D%0AIII. AC Profiles:%0D%0A1. FXS Coefficients assume -6dBr RX (Output from chipset) and 0dB TX relative gain levels.%0D%0A2. Supported countries not individually listed should use the default 600R profile AC_FXS_RF14_600R_DEF.%0D%0A4. AC FXS Coefficients assume the use of two 7 ohm series resistors or PTCs. Customers using other PTC resistance values (such as %0D%0A25ohms or 50 ohms) should not use these AC coefficients and can request alternate ones from Microsemi.%0D%0A5. This release includes both Narrowband and Wideband coefficients. Note that the ZL880 Series devices support per channel Narrowband or %0D%0AWideband audio selection.%0D%0A%0D%0A%0D%0AIV. Ring Profiles:%0D%0A1. RING_ZL880_FB150V_DEF is the default ringing profile and should be used for all countries which do not have a listed ringing profile.  %0D%0AThe default ringing profile is set for a sine wave ringing with an amplitude of 62Vrms (87.7Vpk)with 48V DC bias and a frequency of 25 Hz%0D%0Atracking supply.%0D%0A2. Most ringing profiles on the list are sinusoidal with an amplitude of 62Vrms with 48V DC bias. %0D%0A3. The ringing definitions may be changed based on the requirements of the target market as long as the total amplitude (AC + DC %0D%0Acomponents) does not exceed the limits set forth in the ZL88701/702 data sheet.%0D%0A%0D%0A%0D%0AV. Tone Profiles:%0D%0A1. These profiles are available only in the full version of the VP-API-II.%0D%0A2. The shown levels assume a 6dB attenuation in the chipset before being outputed to line.%0D%0A3. Call progress tone levels may be arbitrary as they are not always specified in national standards, or the standards may not be available %0D%0Ato Microsemi.%0D%0A4. ITU-T Recommendation E.180 (03/1998) revised on 02/2003 and ETSI TR 101 041-2 V.1.1.1 (05/1997) were used if national standards were not%0D%0Aavailable.%0D%0A5. Recommended ETSI ES 201 970 call progress tones are provided for reference.%0D%0A6. Modulated tones f1 x f2 are approximated as the sum of f1 + (f1+f2)/2 + (f1-f2)/2.%0D%0A7. The data in these profiles may be changed by the user as necessary.%0D%0A 8. T_CAS_DEF is not a country-specific tone and is used by several national Caller ID profiles.%0D%0A%0D%0AVI. Cadence Profiles:%0D%0A1. These profiles are available only in the full version of the VP-API-II.%0D%0A2.  ITU-T Recommendation E.180 (03/1998) revised on 02/2003 and ETSI TR 101 041-2 V.1.1.1 (05/1997) were used if national standards were not%0D%0Aavailable.%0D%0A3. Recommended ETSI ES 201 970 call progress cadences are provided for reference.%0D%0A4. Some countries support multiple call progress tone cadences.  The ones used are believed to be representative and most common.  The user may%0D%0Awish to edit some of the cadence definitions or add additional cadences.%0D%0A5. Ringing signal cadences include the alerting signal(s) and necessary delays for Type 1 Caller ID, if it is supported below in the Caller ID %0D%0AProfiles.%0D%0A%0D%0AVII. Caller ID Profiles:%0D%0A1. These profiles are available only in the full version of the VP-API-II.%0D%0A2. The option to calculate the checksum in the VP-API-II is selected for all countries except Japan, which requires that the CRC checksum be %0D%0Acalculated by host application.%0D%0A%0D%0AVIII. Metering Profiles:%0D%0A1. These profiles are available only in the full version of the VP-API-II.%0D%0A2. Metering profiles are provided for 12kHz and 16kHz signaling. They are not currently listed by the countries that use them. %0D%0A%0D%0A(c) Copyright 2012 Microsemi Corporation. All rights reserved.%0D%0A%0D%0A-----------------